WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.480
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain a Hungarian drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:19.200
called “White God”. Watch out and take care!
Lili is a thirteen-year-old girl living in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.560
Hungary. She has a mixed-breed dog named&nbsp;
Hagen. Since Lili’s parents are divorced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:29.840
she hardly gets along with either of them. The&nbsp;
only creature she is close to is her pet dog.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.960
At the beginning of the movie, she plays with the&nbsp;
dog in a park while her mother watches them. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.640
is planning to move to the United States, leaving&nbsp;
Lili to live with her father Daniel permanently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.600
Daniel works in a slaughterhouse and hasn’t&nbsp;
met Lili since she was three years old. He is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.640
surprised that she has brought the dog with her&nbsp;
because his apartment is too small to hold one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:56.240
He is also not fond of pets in general but has to&nbsp;
compromise because of his daughter. When they get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.960
to the building, Daniel’s landlady tells him&nbsp;
that pets are not allowed in the apartment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.680
He quietly says that he will get rid of&nbsp;
it in a few days. Even during dinner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:11.360
Lili disobeys her father, feeding Hagen homemade&nbsp;
food. They have to squeeze in the same room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:16.800
because of the size of the apartment. The dog&nbsp;
has separation anxiety and cannot sleep alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:23.360
but Daniel still locks him in the bathroom. He&nbsp;
cries for a long time, not letting anyone sleep.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:30.080
At last, Lili goes to him and plays Franz Liszt's&nbsp;
"Hungarian Rhapsody No. 2" on her trumpet. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.960
dog calms down after listening to the tune and&nbsp;
Lili sleeps in the bathtub for the night. 
&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.520
The next morning, they are woken up by someone&nbsp;
ringing their doorbell. A man from canine control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:50.960
informs them of a complaint they received about&nbsp;
their dog howling at night. At first, Daniel tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:56.400
to hide the fact that they own a pet but the guy&nbsp;
happens to see Hagen in the apartment. Daniel is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.840
told to pay a large "mongrel" fee imposed by the&nbsp;
Hungarian government because Hagen is a mixed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:07.600
breed. He is strictly against paying money to keep&nbsp;
the dog he doesn’t even want in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.400
That day, Lili takes Hagen to her music&nbsp;
class because her father won’t let him alone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.920
in the house. Since no pets are allowed in the&nbsp;
class, she hides him inside a cabinet used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.520
store instruments. However, when the music&nbsp;
starts to play, a scared Hagen runs outside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.720
Lili’s music teacher asks her to send the dog&nbsp;
away and stay in the classroom but she disobeys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.920
him and walks out. The two are walking through&nbsp;
the street when Daniel stops them, furious at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:39.920
the fact that he was called by her music teacher.&nbsp;
He has decided to get rid of the dog at any cost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:45.280
He asks Lili to give him to the dog shelter but&nbsp;
she stays adamant about keeping him with her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.040
Having had enough of her stubbornness,&nbsp;
he kicks the dog out of the car.
&nbsp;

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:56.400
Lili cries and asks the dog to return but Daniel&nbsp;
forces her inside and drives away. The poor dog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:02.320
chases them, not wanting to let go of his master&nbsp;
but he cannot keep up with the speeding car. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:08.560
the next few hours, he waits in the street for&nbsp;
Lili, but she never returns. At home, Lili wakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.760
up in the middle of the night and gets ready to go&nbsp;
to Hagen but she is found by her father who forces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:19.280
her back to sleep. Hagen wakes up after spending&nbsp;
the night under a bridge. He looks around for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.400
food and finds a dead animal by the side of the&nbsp;
road. After contemplating if he should eat it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:30.800
he decides against it. Following that, he reaches&nbsp;
a butcher shop and looks at the meat longingly. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:36.240
white stray dog catches his attention who he&nbsp;
follows and ends up in the back of the shop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:41.600
Several stray dogs are eating the leftovers but&nbsp;
they bark at Hagen when he tries to get a bite.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:47.440
This attracts the butcher who chases them&nbsp;
away. A naive Hagen stays put in his place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.000
making the butcher even more furious. He is&nbsp;
about to attack the poor dog with a knife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:57.920
but is distracted by the white dog at the right&nbsp;
time. Taking the opportunity, both dogs run away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.720
and reach a puddle where all of the stray dogs&nbsp;
of the area have gathered to drink water. 
&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.280
However, they are soon approached by workers&nbsp;
from animal control who catch them and put&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.800
them in cages. Hagen and his friend manage to&nbsp;
run away while being followed. He is chased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.200
through the streets and eventually saved by&nbsp;
a homeless person. After the workers leave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:23.040
the man forcefully ties a rope around his neck&nbsp;
and keeps him as his pet. In the meantime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.320
Daniel takes Lili back to her music class and&nbsp;
makes her apologize to the teacher for yesterday.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.840
After the class, she secretly goes to the street&nbsp;
where they had left the dog the previous day. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.720
looks for him all around the neighborhood&nbsp;
but to no avail. She also posts posters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.800
of the missing dog everywhere she can. Later at&nbsp;
night, the homeless man sells Hagen to a dealer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:50.880
He is chained with his kind in the back of a&nbsp;
shop. The next morning, a client named Szabolcs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.840
comes looking to buy a dog for dog fighting&nbsp;
competitions. The dealer claims Hagen won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.840 --> 00:05:01.360
be good for fighting because he is a lapdog&nbsp;
but Szabolcs buys him anyway. Hagen is given a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:07.040
sleeping pill which makes him pass out. Following&nbsp;
that, Szabolcs brings him to his house and gives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:13.600
him a mixture of protein powder. To make him more&nbsp;
aggressive, Szabolcs beats him regularly. He is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:19.840
mostly starved and caged the entire day. The only&nbsp;
time he is let out is when Szabolcs trains him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:26.160
If he doesn’t do as told, he is beaten brutally.&nbsp;
The dog’s life has changed for the worse. 
&nbsp;

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:32.240
Szabolcs’s training technique gets tougher every&nbsp;
day. Hagen is no longer the gentle dog he used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:38.960
to be, he eventually turns very aggressive, ready&nbsp;
to be let into the battlefield. In the meantime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.080
Lili continues her search for him. She goes&nbsp;
to a dog shelter and asks its owner about him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:49.600
She is told that he might have been hit by a car&nbsp;
or died in a street fight. Her day gets worse when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:54.480
her bicycle gets stolen from outside the shelter.&nbsp;
That night, Hagen is brought to the fighting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:06:00.000
ground by his master. The rules of the match are&nbsp;
simple; for a dog to win, the other one has to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.920
die. People bet on them and earn a lot of money.&nbsp;
When Szabolcs brings Hagen in, everyone assumes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.200
that he is going to lose. They even tell Szabolcs&nbsp;
he could have done better but the guy is confident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:17.760
about his training. The match between Hagen and a&nbsp;
rottweiler starts. After a fierce fight, both are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:23.360
left bloodied and injured, but at last, Hagen gets&nbsp;
a tight grip on his opponent and wins the match.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:28.720
Impressed by his skills, a dog dealer&nbsp;
approaches Szabolcs wanting to buy him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:34.160
When Szabolcs refuses, they get into an argument.&nbsp;
Amidst it, the lights go off and Hagen takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:39.920
the opportunity to run away. He runs the entire&nbsp;
night, as far as he can from the dog dealers. 
&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:44.720
Lili, on the other hand, is running&nbsp;
home after her bicycle was stolen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.760
She meets a friend from her music class named&nbsp;
Peter. He is about to go to a high school party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.440
which she asks to join. At first, he is reluctant&nbsp;
about bringing her, but he figures she can be used&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.440 --> 00:07:00.000
to carry drugs to the party without being&nbsp;
caught. He makes her hide some pills in her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.160
pocket which she sneaks into the party. Everyone&nbsp;
there is way older than her but Lili doesn’t care.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:11.520
She sits in a corner and watches everyone dance.&nbsp;
By the end of the night, she falls asleep on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:17.200
floor. The next morning, the party is raided by&nbsp;
the police. When Lili is found with drugs, she is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:22.880
taken to the police station. Thankfully, her tests&nbsp;
come out negative so she is allowed to return home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:33.600
with her father. Daniel cries for the first time&nbsp;
in years after seeing his daughter well and alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:39.040
He had been worried to death the previous night.&nbsp;
He apologizes to her for taking Hagen away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:44.880
her and promises to buy her a new dog. Lili&nbsp;
forgives her father and reconciles with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:50.560
after which, they return home happily. Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Hagen reaches the puddle the next morning and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:55.920
reunites with his friend, the white dog. They are&nbsp;
together playing by a river when the people from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:01.280
animal control take them away and put them in a&nbsp;
shelter. Hagen is injured because of the fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:06.960
and is treated for it. He is put in a cage with&nbsp;
hundreds of other stray dogs and given food. 
&nbsp;

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:11.760
While most of the dogs devour it, he doesn’t&nbsp;
even look at the food. The following day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:17.120
people come to the shelter to adopt the dogs of&nbsp;
their choice. A girl seems to like Hagen but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:23.840
barks at her and is aggressive to the workers.&nbsp;
The owner asks him to be put down. Somewhere else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.840 --> 00:08:29.200
Lili is playing the trumpet at a concert with her&nbsp;
orchestra. Daniel is in the audience to cheer for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:33.680
his daughter. Hagen is about to be thrown in&nbsp;
a cage with the other dogs when he attacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:39.520
the dog handler. He grows aggressive and bites&nbsp;
the man on his neck, killing him eventually.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:44.720
The other dogs follow his lead and rush out of&nbsp;
the cage. Since Hagen is the one to free them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:49.760
they make him the leader of the pack. The owner&nbsp;
of the shelter tries to stop him but he pushes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:55.360
her aside and escapes with the others. They&nbsp;
run through the city, ensuing chaos all around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:01.840
People run away to save their lives as the dogs&nbsp;
begin to attack everyone in their way. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:07.120
the dogs also reach the concert that Lili is&nbsp;
playing in. They surround it from all the sides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.240
making the audience barricade themselves within&nbsp;
the auditorium for safety. The performance stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:18.320
as everyone starts to panic. Lili senses that&nbsp;
Hagen is also with them and runs outside despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:24.560
Peter warning her not to. A stranger tells Lili&nbsp;
and Peter to not go downstairs because the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:31.120
city is in lockdown but they do not listen.
At last, she cycles down the empty streets trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:36.880
to find Hagen, believing that she can stop the&nbsp;
havoc. Eventually, a pack of dogs chases behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:42.640
her. She falls to the ground but they ignore her&nbsp;
as if they are on a mission. It turns out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:48.560
Hagen is leading them to all the people who have&nbsp;
hurt him in the past. First, he finds Szabolcs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:55.280
and approaches him. Soon, he is joined by his pack&nbsp;
who attack him, leaving a bloody mess behind. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.280 --> 00:10:00.880
Lili gets to the location, they have already left.&nbsp;
A policeman finds her and puts her in the car.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:07.360
However, she escapes and cycles away looking for&nbsp;
Hagen yet again. She reaches a meat shop and finds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:13.200
the butcher dead on the floor. He was the same guy&nbsp;
who had tried to kill Hagen earlier in the movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.880
She calls Daniel and asks him to stay inside at&nbsp;
any cost. He, on the other hand, is worried about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:24.400
her safety. Somewhere else, the police force&nbsp;
shoots and kills several dogs but more of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:29.680
keep on coming. The pack goes to the dealer who&nbsp;
had sold Hagen in the market and kills him as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:36.240
well. Now, their last target is Daniel. Lili&nbsp;
cycles back to her home and finds the landlady&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:41.440
dead. She freaks out and runs to her apartment,&nbsp;
finally realizing what Hagen is trying to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:46.800
Knowing that her father’s life is also in&nbsp;
danger, she runs back to the auditorium. 
&nbsp;

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:52.320
Daniel sees her safe and is relieved. However,&nbsp;
Lili is soon approached by Hagen who appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:56.880
to have forgotten her after everything he&nbsp;
has been through. As he growls at Lili,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:02.240
his army joins him. They are about to attack&nbsp;
her when Daniel comes forward with a blowtorch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:08.240
to distract them and save his daughter. When&nbsp;
they still do not calm down, Lili plays Franz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:14.720
Liszt's "Hungarian Rhapsody No. 2" on her trumpet.&nbsp;
Hagen finally remembers her because of the tune.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:21.040
He calms down and the pack follows his lead. They&nbsp;
all lay on the ground, listening to her play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:32.080
Daniel is shocked and relieved at the fact she is&nbsp;
safe. At last, she also lays on the ground with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:37.920
the dogs. The movie ends as Daniel joins them. 
